          "chunk_index": 0,
          "text": "Research Laboratories at the Halvorsen Institute of Technology\n\n> Synthetic demonstration document. The laboratories, people and figures described here are fictional.\nRetrieval and Reasoning Lab\n\nThe Retrieval and Reasoning Lab (RRL) belongs to the School of Computing and is located on the third\nfloor of Aster Hall. It was founded in 2016 and is led by Dr. Lena Park. The lab has 14 members: three\nfaculty members, eight doctoral students and three research engineers. In 2024 its research funding was\n2.4 million euros, about 70 percent of which came from the Nordic Research Council.\n\nThe lab runs two main projects. Project Veritas, started in 2022, develops methods that check whether\nstatements generated by language models are supported by source documents. Project Atlas, started in\n2023, studies multi-hop retrieval for questions that need information from several documents.\nGrid Storage Lab",
